 "version": "lineage-tag-family-cases-0.3",
 "about": "0.3 (operator ruling 2026-10-29, the narrow platform rule): the 0.2 family, unchanged, then, when the prerelease names a platform, '@' and its platform tokens. The 0.2 family: drop build metadata (after the first '+'); no '-' => 'release'; otherwise the prerelease is everything after the first '-': a first identifier (up to the first '.') that is lower-case hex [0-9a-f], 7 to 40 characters, with at least one digit => 'num' (a commit hash); else the leading run of ASCII letters [A-Za-z]+, lower-cased; no leading letter => 'num'. The platform tokens: split the prerelease on '.' and '-', lower-case each token, keep the tokens that are exactly one of platform_tokens, each once, in order of first appearance, joined by '-'. None => the 0.2 family alone. 'release' never gains a suffix. So executor's 15 KB shim 2.0.0-beta.25 is 'beta' and its 480 MB build 2.0.0-beta.25-darwin-arm64 is 'beta@darwin-arm64': a platform build's predecessor is the previous build for the same platform. platform_tokens is closed: a new token is a new fixture version.",
